 gets into contact with his  agent who tells him that Disney was  looking to bring on a director to get a  Kingdom Hearts TV show off the ground  Seth had a meeting with Disney they gave  Seth a copy of Kingdom Hearts 1 and then  he blitzes through the entire game in a  week and decides you know what the sword  gets pretty cool I'm in soon after  Disney showed set the script of the  Kingdom Hearts pilot and to quote Seth  after finishing the game I read the  script for the pilot it read like an  episode of Aladdin co-star the  characters from Kingdom Hearts I told  them I wanted to rewrite the script to  put the Kingdom Hearts characters at the  center of the story I was fired wow  Disney meddling with Kingdom Hearts to  force the main cast to take a backseat  see a focus on selling you on their  films  who could ever have foreseen this so  yeah Seth was fired but he really wanted  to work on Kingdom Hearts so he went to  the head of the studio and pled his case  and it turns out the head of the studio  was the guy who would pitch the idea for  the cage cartoon in the first place and  so Seth was rehired and he got to react  script to be much closer to the show  that he wanted to make and so with the  project greenlit Seth got to work on  boarding the pilot for Kingdom Hearts  Seth remarks during the production that  he took a good amount of inspiration  from Cowboy Bebop at the time wanting to  get across the same feeling of  loneliness spike in the crew had while  drifting through space as Sora would be  traversing from world to world with the  crushing Solitude of not being able to  find his friends Seth did The Impossible  he made the gummy ship from Kingdom  Hearts 1 interesting but Seth also  comments on a whole host of other  problems during production including  Disney not allowing the pilot to act as  An Origin episode so Seth had to cram  the origin of Sora and the Gang  alongside the plot of an already  existing episode in 11 short minutes and  then when 