e writing this video I  always really liked Eight Crazy Nights  but I had no idea who Seth Kearsley was  until doing my research for this video  and uh I found out he uh also did a lot  of work on uh the Looney Tunes Show  which I think is one of the best  cartoons ever made and uh man Seth is  this amazing dude you should go follow  him on YouTube and Seth if you somehow  ever see this I'd love to buy you a  drink from one artist to another thank  you and so on October 11th 2022 almost  20 years after it was first produced  Seth released the pilot for Kingdom  Hearts on his YouTube channel is uh what  I would say but literally in the middle  of editing this video Disney took the  pilot down from Seth's Channel no yeah  uh we can't have nice things I guess uh  so uh no yeah uh back to the video but  as for the episode itself I absolutely  love it it does a great job of staying  faithful to the look and feel of the  original Kingdom Hearts the artwork is  surprisingly polished for an animatic  maid essentially by one guy and then  there's some scenes where their  roughness genuinely brought me to tears  with how much I was gackling like  look at this big on I am more than  [Music]  that it's so interrupt  and then there's Riku Riku is an [ __ ]  and I love it look at this [ __ ] eating  grin he literally spends the entire  episode just gaslighting Sora and acting  like a gigantic piece of [ __ ] which to  be fair is pretty on brand for Kingdom  Hearts 1 Riku but yeah this pilot is  amazing they even managed to get the  original voice cast to reprise their  roles from Kingdom Hearts 1 with the  sole exception being Sora due to Haley  Joel Osment not being available during  the time of recording looking back on  this pilot this time capsule of  Animation from the early 2000s it  honestly makes me sad that Disney passed  on this at the time of me writing this  video Disney has teased a Kingdom Hearts  show that'll be airing on Disney plus  and while I am hopeful for that it still  [ __ ] sucks that Seth's version with  all of his passion ended up getting  buried by the whim of Executives but at  the same time I'm grateful that Seth  finally released it after all these  years a pilot brought to light for a  show that never was but that's enough  for handling anime thank you all so much  for watching this video I really  appreciate it as per usual if you like  what we do feel free to drop a like  comment and hit that subscribe button  and if you like me you can follow me on  Twitch Twitter and YouTube at Red  Muffler Man and uh yeah have a good one  everybody take it easy

